Selection means the program chooses what to do according to a condition. A condition is either true or false.

mark = 72
if mark >= 70:
    print("Distinction")
elif mark >= 50:
    print("Pass")
else:
    print("Try again")

This prints Distinction. Python checks the conditions in order and runs only the first matching block. The spaces at the start of a line, called indentation, show which lines belong to each block. Missing indentation causes an error in Python.

