Structured Query Language (SQL) is the common language for this. Consider this query on a table called Students:

SELECT Name, Mark
FROM Students
WHERE Mark >= 50
ORDER BY Mark DESC;

SELECT names the fields to show. FROM names the table. WHERE sets the condition. ORDER BY sorts the results, and DESC means largest first.

Other commands change data:

INSERT INTO Students (Name, Mark) VALUES ('Wanjiru', 68);
UPDATE Students SET Mark = 70 WHERE StudentID = 12;
DELETE FROM Students WHERE StudentID = 12;

Always use WHERE with UPDATE and DELETE. Without it, every record is changed or removed.

