CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets. A rule picks an element and sets its style.

h1 {
  color: blue;
  font-size: 24px;
}

This makes all h1 headings blue, with a text size of 24 pixels. Keeping CSS in a separate file means that one change can update a whole website.

Good web pages load fast, work on phones, and are easy to read and navigate. Compress images, because large images are slow to load on a weak connection.

